1.  clone this repo 
2.  $ build -t comp_nginx_image ./nginx_geoip
3.  $ docker run -d --name comp_nginx --network comp_network -p 80:80 comp_nginx_image
4.  $ docker ps
# there's should be 3 containers:
#     a. comp_postgres
#     b. comp_fastapi
#     c. comp_nginx
#     if not - watch docker_containers readme
5.  $ cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:80
# there's should be smth like that:
# 2025-04-05T16:36:51Z INF +--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
# 2025-04-05T16:36:51Z INF |  Your quick Tunnel has been created! Visit it at (it may take some time to be reachable):  |
# 2025-04-05T16:36:51Z INF |  https://teachers-statewide-assigned-listing.trycloudflare.com                             |
# 2025-04-05T16:36:51Z INF +--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
6.  fastapi has 2 requests: get_data, pull_data;
        to test you need to combine: Cloudflare Tunnel URL + / + fastapi request and paste it into browser
7.  to test it locally without cloudfare:
        change: CF-Connecting-IP -> X-Forwarded-For
        and paste this comand into terminal: curl -H "X-Forwarded-For: <some ip>" http://localhost/get_data -v
